The conversion modules independently express the official architecture using
static Core ML-compatible graphs. Reference implementation details and source
revisions are recorded in the workspace research documents. Model weights are
downloaded separately and are not included in this Python distribution.

Optional forced alignment uses Qwen3-ForcedAligner-0.6B (Apache-2.0) through
the separately installed qwen-asr runtime. That runtime and its dependencies
retain their own licenses; their distributions are not included in this wheel.
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-ForcedAligner-0.6B
https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-ASR
https://github.com/lovit/soynlp/blob/master/LICENSE

Optional CPU diarization uses sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0), a separately acquired
pyannote segmentation model (MIT), and a 3D-Speaker embedding model
(Apache-2.0). Model identities, revisions, hashes, and license references are
recorded in the acquisition metadata and diarization documentation.
https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
https://huggingface.co/pyannote/segmentation-3.0
https://github.com/modelscope/3D-Speaker
